From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:00:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] ci: mirror the folders to the old repositories through
 pull requests

During the monorepo trial the old repositories are read-only mirrors. tools/mirror.py, run by .github/workflows/mirror.yml on every push to main and nightly, keeps a branch monorepo-mirror in each old repository with one commit per monorepo commit that changes the folder (shared-data symlinks become submodule pointers to the mirrored data repositories), opens one pull request per repository, and, once its CI passes, fast-forwards its main and pushes the translated tags; that only when the repository variable MIRROR_MERGE is true (set by hand after switchover) and the old repository is locked (<prefix>-vX.Y.Z -> vX.Y.Z). Before switchover only the branch and a draft PR are written. The old CI result comes back as a mirror/<repo> commit status, and an issue tracks red old CI.

- pr-checks.yml: mirror-check, every folder can be mirrored (no stray symlinks leaving a package).
- DEVELOPING.md: the old repositories, the trial rules, porting changes; README and PR template pointers.
